.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-split 1  "ngx-split " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-split \- Split a file that defines several sites into one file per site (so each can be edited on its own)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-split\fR [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISITE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Split a file that defines several sites into one file per site (so each can be edited on its own)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show the plan without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISITE\fR>
Site ID (from `ngx ls`) or any of its domain names
.SH EXTRA
Server blocks are moved as they are; upstreams, maps and other shared directives stay in the original file.

Example:
  sudo ngx split 5
